@startuml VIS04DomainModelExcerpt
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide methods

title Domain Model Excerpt - VIS04 Textures and Materials (read-only view of WEB06 concepts)

note as N0
    Every concept below is OWNED by WEB06 (usWEB06 section 2.5; persisted in PostgreSQL,
    layout stored as JSONB). VIS04 introduces NO new domain concept: it reads the
    ACTIVE configuration loaded by VIS01 (GET /kitchen-configurations/active) and maps
    MaterialProperties and the resolved KitchenAssets to 3D rendering materials.
    Only the concepts relevant to materials and textures are shown.
    The WEB06 back end is the authority on these rules.
end note

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' KITCHEN CONFIGURATION AGGREGATE (WEB06) - Material & Texture perspective
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Kitchen Configuration Aggregate (WEB06)" <<Rectangle>> {

    class KitchenConfiguration <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
        + version : Integer
    }
    note right of KitchenConfiguration
        VIS01 renders ONLY the configuration
        with status = ACTIVE; VIS04 builds the
        materials of that configuration.
    end note

    class KitchenConfigurationId <<vo>> {
        + value : String
    }

    enum ConfigurationStatus <<enum>> {
        ACTIVE
        INACTIVE
    }

    class KitchenLayout <<vo>> {
    }
    note left of KitchenLayout
        Floor and walls have a texture set
        (WEB06: MATERIAL_REQUIRED; VIS04 BR 6).
        Room surfaces have UVs in metres
        (VIS02 D7).
    end note

    class SceneElement <<entity>> {
        + elementId : String
        + name : String [0..1]
    }
    note bottom of SceneElement
        Each object type (VIS02 equipment, VIS03
        assembly-line part) has its own texture set;
        elements of the same type vary through
        color / roughness / metalness (AC 1, BR 1).
        Procedural: material mandatory (BR 6).
        Asset: material optional = override (BR 8, BR 9).
    end note

    enum ElementCategory <<enum>> {
        EQUIPMENT
        ASSEMBLY_LINE
    }

    abstract class ModelReference <<vo>> {
        + source : "ASSET" | "PROCEDURAL"
    }

    class ProceduralModelReference <<vo>> {
        + shape : "BOX" | "CYLINDER" | "SPHERE" | "DOME"
        + size : Vector3
    }

    class AssetModelReference <<vo>> {
        + assetId : KitchenAssetId
    }

    class MaterialProperties <<vo>> {
        + color : String [0..1]
        + roughness : Decimal [0..1]
        + metalness : Decimal [0..1]
        + colorMapAssetId : String [0..1]
        + roughnessMapAssetId : String [0..1]
        + normalMapAssetId : String [0..1]
        + bumpMapAssetId : String [0..1]
    }
    note right of MaterialProperties
        **Texture set (BR 6, AC 3):** colorMapAssetId AND one of
        roughness / normal / bump map is MANDATORY when
        - the material is required (floor, walls, procedural), or
        - the material contains any *MapAssetId
        (a partial set is rejected, WEB06).
        A scalar-only material (e.g. { "color": "#aa0000" }) is
        valid on an asset: it tints the model's own materials (D6).
        **Values (BR 15):** color #RRGGBB; roughness, metalness in [0, 1].
        Absent values: #ffffff / 1 / 0 (BR 16).
        Normal + bump together are allowed (D10).
        Color map in sRGB; other maps linear (BR 17).
    end note

    KitchenConfiguration "1" *-- "1" KitchenConfigurationId : identified by >
    KitchenConfiguration "1" --> "1" ConfigurationStatus : current status >
    KitchenConfiguration "1" *-- "1" KitchenLayout : content >
    KitchenLayout "1" *-- "2..300" SceneElement : contains >
    SceneElement "1" --> "1" ElementCategory : belongs to >
    SceneElement "1" *-- "1" ModelReference : represented by >
    SceneElement "1" *-- "0..1" MaterialProperties : rendered with >
    ModelReference <|-- ProceduralModelReference
    ModelReference <|-- AssetModelReference
}

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' KITCHEN ASSET AGGREGATE (WEB06) - Texture and model assets resolved into URLs
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Kitchen Asset Aggregate (WEB06)" <<Rectangle>> {

    class KitchenAsset <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
        + format : String
        + path : String
        + embeddedTextureSet : boolean [0..1]
    }
    note right of KitchenAsset
        Resolved in the response map as
        assets[assetId] = { kind, format, url }.
        Existence and kind are checked by the VIS01
        activeConfigurationParser (BR 13).
        embeddedTextureSet (MODEL only): every material
        of the model has a colour map + roughness /
        normal map. If false, elements using the model
        need a material override with a texture set
        (MODEL_TEXTURES_MISSING, BR 7).
        Source textures and models stay owned by
        LoadedAssets (VIS01); VIS04 only clones them
        (BR 10).
    end note

    class KitchenAssetId <<vo>> {
        + value : String
    }

    enum AssetKind <<enum>> {
        MODEL
        TEXTURE
    }

    KitchenAsset "1" *-- "1" KitchenAssetId : identified by >
    KitchenAsset "1" --> "1" AssetKind : is a >
}

MaterialProperties ..> KitchenAsset : refers to texture maps\n(kind = TEXTURE) >
AssetModelReference ..> KitchenAsset : refers to 3D model\n(kind = MODEL) >

@enduml